# living_docs_lint.rish -- ratchet-advisory living-docs lint (eight duties).
#
# WHAT THIS IS FOR. The tree's living pages carry promises a reader can follow: a link
# that opens, a page the roster names, a word the Lexicon still seats, a size small
# enough to read in one sitting. This runs eight small readings over those pages and
# prints what it finds. It advises and never refuses, so a lap reads it and chooses.
#
# Kaeden seated the name 20260712.222800 - Claude counsel at bench 4fa8363.
# Print every parity run; never fail. Hardening horizon: link-breaks may earn
# a gate once the docs shelf proves stable.
#
# Duties (fixtures/living_docs_lint_scan.rish - .sh body via run seam):
#   1. retired LEXICON words in living-voice lines (word-boundary; keeps.txt exemptions)
#   2. broken relative links on roster
#   3. orphan roster pages (no inbound from roster + docs/README)
#   4. Status rooms on rostered living pages
#   5. docs/ pin-strings byte-match canon (PUBKEYS - master-seal - exit card)
#   6. living pin size <= living_pin_max_bytes, read from the seated law by
#      tools/fixtures/l/living_pin_max_bytes.sh; near-bound (>=90% of the page's OWN bound) names
#      fold + SEASONS roster, its remaining headroom, and the count of paths weighed. The weighed
#      set is the docs roster UNION the seated pin roster
#      (tools/fixtures/l/living_pin_guard_roster.txt) -- four of the seven seated pins stood outside
#      this duty until REDS %396. Gated by tools/l/living_pin_near_bound_witness.rish.
#   7. tools/**/*.py count -- target zero (Python-at-seam law)
#   8. shell bodies (>40 lines) beneath .rish wrappers -- harvest ratchet (only falls)
#
# First-lap roster: tools/fixtures/l/living_docs_lint_roster.sh
# Design: active-designing/date/20260712/20260712-221600_docs-compression-layer-design.md
# Pin law: context/specs/20260724-132812_pin-and-ledger-living-pin-max-bytes.md
# Growth law: context/specs/append-only-growth-law.md
# Python law: context/specs/20260724-143155_python-at-the-seam-law.md
# Shell harvest: counsel/date/20260725/20260725-040247_what-the-shell-remembers.md
#
# Missing Rishi verb (this wrapper's body): accumulate - filter chained - read bounded
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/l/living_docs_lint.rish

say "living-docs lint: ratchet advisory (eight duties)…"
let scan = run ["rishi/bin/rishi" "run" "tools/fixtures/l/living_docs_lint_scan.rish"]
say scan.out
say "GREEN: living-docs lint — advisories printed; witness never fails."
